          },
          "mechanism": "Asthma diagnosis indicates underlying airway reactivity and inflammatory tendency. These same inflammatory pathways may relate to menstrual cycle regularity through immune-endocrine interactions and also directly increase risk of COPD as part of a shared obstructive airway disease predisposition.",
          "justification": "Asthma captures common underlying inflammatory/immune status that affects both exposure and outcome.",
          "role": "confounder",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
        {
          "variable": {
            "kind": "variable",
            "key": "m2:Q7.4",
