          "mechanism": "Time to menstrual regularity is a direct downstream consequence of pubertal development and menstrual maturation. The exposure (m2:Q9.3) is explicitly conditioned on periods having become regular, so this variable is on the causal pathway from puberty to the establishment of regular cycles and measurement of cycle length.",
